          "Period panties sit outside the body — the simplest option, and the most comfortable for overnight and sensitive days. Tampons and cups sit inside: change a tampon every 4–8 hours and empty a cup every 8–12 hours, because leaving either in too long carries a small risk of toxic shock syndrome (TSS). Many people mix and match — a cup or tampon by day, and an Ovy period panty overnight or as a reliable backup.",
